WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.200
A mobile task force makes its way through
the Siberian forest.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:10.260
Snow covers the trees; the only light comes
from the moon shining through the branches.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.660
The commander holds up a hand signaling the
team to halt.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.109
In a small clearing in front of them is the
creature they’ve been searching for.

00:00:18.109 --> 00:00:20.939
It appears to be part-deer, part-human.

00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:24.599
The creature howls in pain as it rips the
skin from its body.

00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:30.170
The SCP agents watch in horror as the creature
reaches its arm high into the air and plunges

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.180
a knife into its stomach.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.700
It doubles over in pain and stops screaming.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:39.640
The creature pulls the knife from its midsection
and stands upright.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.620
Blood splatters across the shimmering, white,
snow.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:46.870
It turns towards the mobile task force and
slowly walks toward them.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:49.050
“Help me,” the creature whispers.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:53.000
“I need you to save me from what’s inside.”

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.010
It collapses to the ground.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:59.150
The mobile task force secures the creature
in a containment vehicle in preparation for

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:01.120
further examination.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:06.799
This is SCP-1068-RU - Shell of God.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:12.229
When they arrive with the creature to an undisclosed
SCP Foundation site location, Dr. Belkov is

00:01:12.229 --> 00:01:15.070
put in charge of learning more about the entity.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:21.280
When SCP-1068 first awakens in its containment
chamber Belkov is watching from behind a two-way

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.280
mirror.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.429
The creature walks up to the mirror and examines
the countless scars and stitches that cover

00:01:26.429 --> 00:01:27.990
its body.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:33.539
SCP-1068 shakes its head and gingerly runs
a long finger along the fresh wound where

00:01:33.539 --> 00:01:35.139
it stabbed itself earlier.

00:01:35.139 --> 00:01:40.310
It glances around the room as if looking for
something, then turns back towards the two-way

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:41.310
glass.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:42.310
“What time is it?”

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:43.509
it asks its reflection.

00:01:43.509 --> 00:01:46.850
Dr. Belkov knows that the creature is talking
to him.

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:51.299
It may not know who is watching him, but it
knows there is someone there.

00:01:51.299 --> 00:01:53.880
Dr. Belkov pauses for a moment.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.779
What harm can it do to tell it the time? he
thinks.

00:01:56.779 --> 00:01:59.159
Belkov pushes the intercom button and speaks.

00:01:59.159 --> 00:02:04.020
“You’ve been in there for almost six hours,”
he says into the microphone.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.210
SCP-1068 looks startled.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.319
Its eyes open wide as it scans the room again.

00:02:08.319 --> 00:02:09.840
“You need to let me out of here!”

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:10.840
it shouts.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.140
“Quickly, or you all will be in danger!”

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:18.000
The creature starts to bang on the glass causing
Dr. Belkov to take a few steps back.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.110
There is fear in its eyes that terrifies the
doctor.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:24.770
Belkov tentatively walks back towards the
intercom button and pushes it.

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:27.910
“I am not sure it’d be safe to let you
out quite yet my friend.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.720
Why don’t you tell me what’s going on?”

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.879
“There is no time!”

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:33.540
SCP-1068 screams.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.870
“I can feel him coming.”

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:40.130
Just as it finishes the sentence SCP-1068
stumbles backward.

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:46.110
Dr. Belkov looks on in horror as the creature’s
stomach begins to expand—as if something

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:48.290
is pushing on it from the inside.

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:51.780
A set of claws rips through its skin from
within.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:54.430
Warning lights begin to flash in the observation
room.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:57.700
The temperature around SCP-1068 has plummeted.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.630
The fluorescents in the containment chamber
start to flicker.

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:05.400
The howls of the creature are accompanied
by the screeching of something else.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:11.439
Whoever is trying to crawl out of SCP-1068
is fighting hard to complete their task.

00:03:11.439 --> 00:03:15.430
SCP-1068 swings the knife tied around its
wrist into its hand.

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:20.000
It begins stabbing at whatever is trying to
burst out of it, causing blood and skin to

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.819
be thrown across the room.

00:03:21.819 --> 00:03:25.120
The creature opens its mouth and lets out
a cry of pain.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:30.239
This goes on for several minutes before whatever
is inside SCP-1068 retreats back to where

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:32.090
it came from.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:34.760
SCP-1068 stands in the room panting.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:38.659
It opens the satchel at its waist and pulls
out a bone needle and string.

00:03:38.659 --> 00:03:41.760
It meticulously begins to sew up the wounds
from the knife.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.019
Dr. Belkov watches.

00:03:44.019 --> 00:03:46.260
Panic fills him as he slams the intercom button.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.569
“What the hell was that?” he asks.

00:03:48.569 --> 00:03:51.209
“That, my dear friend, was my brother.”

00:03:51.209 --> 00:03:56.420
With those words hanging in the air Dr. Belkov
furiously jots down notes.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:57.980
He needs to learn more.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:03.150
Belkov runs out of the observation room and
grabs two SCP agents to accompany him into

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.950
the chamber of SCP-1068.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:10.239
He needs to examine the creature and find
out what is going on within it.

00:04:10.239 --> 00:04:16.519
When Dr. Belkov and the two agents enter the
room, SCP-1068 shows no signs of aggression.

00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:21.440
Although the creature has a masculine voice,
its chest and other human parts seem to be

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:22.440
female.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.930
Its entire body is covered in stitched-up
wounds.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:31.280
However, Dr. Belkov can see into one of the
fresh punctures that SCP-1068 made to itself.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.120
The creature looks at him and shakes its head.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.650
“You have no idea how much danger you are
in,” it says.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:38.100
“We want to help you.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:41.160
My name is Dr. Belkov and I work for the SCP
Foundation.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:43.940
Can I examine that wound?”

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:46.729
SCP-1068 looks at the doctor, considering
his question.

00:04:46.729 --> 00:04:48.190
“I have nothing to hide.

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:50.860
But be aware, you might not like what you
see.”

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:53.069
Dr. Belkov nods his head.

00:04:53.069 --> 00:04:57.449
He holds up a flashlight and shines it into
SCP-1068’s wound.

00:04:57.449 --> 00:04:59.780
What he sees gives him pause.

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:04.449
There are no bones, organs, or muscles of
any type under the creature’s skin.

00:05:04.449 --> 00:05:07.880
The space inside the body seems to be infinite.

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:12.039
Perhaps it is a deep void to another dimension,
Belkov thinks.

00:05:12.039 --> 00:05:16.920
As he gets closer to the wound he can feel
a cold breeze leaving SCP-1068’s body.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.380
“Do you mind?”

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:21.120
Belkov asks while holding up a thermometer.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.990
The creature shrugs indifferently.

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:27.360
Belkov tries to take the temperature just
beneath the creature’s skin, but it is so

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:31.419
cold that it causes the mercury in the thermometer
to freeze.

00:05:31.419 --> 00:05:35.130
The doctor furiously writes notes into his
log.

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:37.780
SCP-1068 finishes stitching up its wounds.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:39.580
The creature sits back in its chair.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:41.419
“I am sure you have some questions.

00:05:41.419 --> 00:05:43.620
Let me start by introducing myself.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:44.620
I am Ay Neil.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:48.949
I come from an ancient tribe that inhabited
the area where you found me many moons ago.”

00:05:48.949 --> 00:05:51.030
“So, you’ve been around for a while?”

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.030
Belkov asks.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:53.030
“That is correct.

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:57.530
I lived with my seven brothers and a small
tribe of humans deep in the Siberian Arctic.

00:05:57.530 --> 00:06:01.110
My brothers and I were wiser and more skilled
than anyone else in the tribe.

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:03.470
We eventually became deities to them.

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:07.419
I was the patron saint of seamstresses and
a warming shoulder for the people.

00:06:07.419 --> 00:06:09.840
Unfortunately, not all of my brothers were
kind.”

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:13.110
“I think I see where this is going,” says
Dr. Belkov.

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:17.840
“In my experience, there is always one who
betrays the rest when it comes to beings with

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:18.960
special powers.”

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:22.819
“You may be more right than you know,”
says Ay Neil, shaking his head.

00:06:22.819 --> 00:06:27.160
“For a long time there was peace and harmony,
but then the Great Grief happened.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:31.319
My brother, whom I will not speak the name
of, was the master of the hunt.

00:06:31.319 --> 00:06:36.039
He believed that since he provided life-sustaining
sustenance for everyone he should be the ruler

00:06:36.039 --> 00:06:37.050
of the tribe.

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:41.080
I was closest to this brother, so he asked
me to join him as his second in command.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.110
I refused.”

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:45.930
“I assume that probably didn’t make him
too happy,” says Belkov.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:47.530
“No, it did not.

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:52.300
He was furious and slaughtered everyone in
the tribe including the women and children.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.280
Then he began to kill his own brothers.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:57.720
He butchered our whole family and then eventually
came for me too.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:01.039
I could not match his combat skills, but I
had a plan.

00:07:01.039 --> 00:07:05.789
We battled for many nights; I waited for the
perfect opportunity, and when my brother lunged

00:07:05.789 --> 00:07:10.030
at me in blind rage and frustration, I knew
it was the moment I was waiting for.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:13.010
I ripped open my stomach and he fell into
the void.”

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:15.889
“I think I’m going to be sick,” gags
Belkov.

00:07:15.889 --> 00:07:19.470
“Are you telling me that thing inside you
is your brother?”

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:22.199
“That is exactly what I am saying,” sighs
Ay Neil.

00:07:22.199 --> 00:07:25.280
“How long has it been in you?” asks Belkov.

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:26.550
“Too long.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:29.810
That is why I have sought the help of the
SCP Foundation.

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:33.510
My brother cannot escape; otherwise, the whole
world will be doomed.”

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:36.810
Dr. Belkov leans back in his chair and whistles.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:41.229
He can’t believe what he is hearing, but
at the same time, this wouldn’t be the craziest

00:07:41.229 --> 00:07:43.389
thing he has witnessed at the Foundation.

00:07:43.389 --> 00:07:46.150
“Now you must leave the room,” says Ay
Neil.

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:49.060
“It is almost time for my brother to try
and escape again.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:53.580
It happens every six hours, and if I do not
stop him, he will destroy us all.”

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:56.510
Dr. Belkov and the agents leave the room.

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:59.550
Once the door is closed Ay Neil begins to
scream.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:03.330
He looks down at his stomach as his brother
rips through his insides.

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:08.639
An audio recorder in the room picks up a conversation
between Ay Neil and his brother as they battle;

00:08:08.639 --> 00:08:11.189
they are talking in their native language.

00:08:11.189 --> 00:08:16.189
Several days later Dr. Belkov retrieves the
audio and sends the recording to the linguistics

00:08:16.189 --> 00:08:18.199
department to be decoded.

00:08:18.199 --> 00:08:23.139
For several days Dr. Belkov watches Ay Neil
battle his brother every six hours.

00:08:23.139 --> 00:08:28.310
The brother rips through the stomach lining
of SCP-1068 with its claws, Ay Neil stabs

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:33.279
him using his knife, and after the bloody
battle is over, Ay Neil sews himself up and

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:35.769
rests until the next attempted escape.

00:08:35.769 --> 00:08:40.440
Dr. Belkov sits in the observation room flipping
through his notes when he comes across a report

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:42.360
from the linguistics department.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:46.890
He had forgotten all about the recording,
but as he reads the translation, his heart

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:47.890
sinks.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:50.040
“What in the name of God?” he says out
loud.

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:53.470
The conversation that was recorded during
the battle didn’t make any sense.

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:57.790
A muffled voice could be heard saying
“think it over, fool.

00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:02.089
Because of your selfishness, we will all die.

00:09:02.089 --> 00:09:05.570
The cycle must not be broken.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:08.310
Let me be reborn.”

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:11.450
This was clearly the pleading of Ay Neil’s
brother.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:15.529
But it is the next words that truly terrify
Dr. Belkov.

00:09:15.529 --> 00:09:17.959
“They believe your lies.

00:09:17.959 --> 00:09:21.010
Isn't that enough for you?”

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:25.320
The next sounds that the recorder picked up
were the stabbing of flesh and screams of

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:26.320
pain.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:28.060
Dr. Belkov shakes his head.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:30.430
So, Ay Neil is lying about something?

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:31.750
Belkov thinks.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:33.360
Could he be evil?

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:35.980
Perhaps the characters in his story were switched…

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:38.600
what if Ay Neil was the one who slaughtered—.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:43.640
Before he can finish his thought there is
a loud crash as the two-way mirror shatters.

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:46.640
Standing in the opening is SCP-1068.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:50.060
His eyes have changed; now they are filled
with evil.

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:54.980
“Oh doctor, I’m sorry it has to come to
this, but I can’t let you live when you

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:58.589
are so close to the truth,” says Ay Neil.

00:09:58.589 --> 00:10:01.540
The creature steps through the opening into
the observation room.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:05.930
Dr. Belkov screams as the knife plunges into
his stomach.

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:11.089
Now watch “SCP-2273 - Major Alexei Belitrov
(SCP Animation).”

00:10:11.089 --> 00:10:15.610
Or check out “SCP-610 - The Flesh That Hates
(SCP Animation).”

